Expanding with index notation and contracting epsilons,
$ (bold(a) times bold(b)) dot (bold(b) times bold(c)) & = epsilon_(i j k) a_j b_k epsilon_(i p q) b_p c_q \
 & = (delta_(j p) delta_(k q) - delta_(j q) delta_(k p)) a_j b_k b_p c_q \
 & = (bold(a) dot bold(b))(bold(b) dot bold(c)) - (bold(a) dot bold(c)) abs(bold(b))^2. $
